\DOC LOCAL_SUB_4_TAC

\TYPE {LOCAL_SUB_4_TAC : int -> string list -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Advances a symbolic {eventually} execution goal across one inlined
modular-subtraction subroutine, replacing the current symbolic state with a
successor state and recording the subroutine's result as a new assumption.

\DESCRIBE
The tactic takes an {int} selecting which occurrence/instance of the subroutine
block to step over, and a {string list} of variable names: the first is the
fresh variable standing for the computed result, and the remaining two identify
the input operands. The conclusion's {eventually} postcondition is left
unchanged, but its state argument is replaced by a fresh successor state
variable. Every assumption mentioning the old state — the program-counter
value, {bytes_loaded}, register reads, memory-content reads, and the
accumulated {MAYCHANGE} frame relating the initial state to the current one —
is discharged and re-added for the new state, with the program-counter
assumption updated to the new code offset and the {MAYCHANGE} frame extended by
the components written by the stepped-over block; assumptions not mentioning
the state (nonoverlapping facts, previously established result
characterisations) are kept as they are. Two assumptions are added: one stating
that a read of the destination memory block in the new state equals the newly
introduced result variable, and one implication stating that if the two input
operands are below the modulus then the result is below twice the modulus and
congruent to their difference modulo it.
{
   A ?- eventually step (\s. P s) s_old
   =================================================  LOCAL_SUB_4_TAC n ["res"; "op1"; "op2"]
   A' , read dest s_new = res ,
        (op1 < m /\ op2 < m
         ==> res < 2 * m /\ (res == op1 - op2) (mod m))
     ?- eventually step (\s. P s) s_new
}
\noindent where {A'} is {A} with the state-dependent assumptions (program
counter, {bytes_loaded}, register and memory reads, {MAYCHANGE} frame) restated
for {s_new}, the program-counter offset updated and the {MAYCHANGE} frame
extended.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, only this single kind of transformation occurs, on
goals of this symbolic-execution form.

\ENDDOC
